  "id": "Compound::DB00786 - Gene::8510",
  "verbalization": "Marimastat is shown to bind to multiple MMPs (Matrix Metalloproteinases) through distinct molecular interactions, with the specific targets Mmp21, Mmp26, and Mmp27 all participating in the same pathway of matrix metalloproteinase activity. These MMPs are known to be involved in the regulation of extracellular matrix remodeling, a process implicated in various pathological conditions. The shared involvement of these MMPs in the pathway to Mmp23b suggests a potential mechanistic link between Marimastat and Mmp23b, where the inhibition of MMP activity may influence the expression or function of Mmp23b. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust and reliable relationship, supported by the shared biological context of MMP-mediated processes. The integration of these findings suggests that Marimastat may exert its effects through a mechanism that modulates MMP activity, potentially affecting Mmp23b through a downstream regulatory pathway.",
